  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building justice and peace through JUST WORLD in Uganda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">JUST WORLD will empower youth (age 13-30), including youth with disabilities,  in Kiryandongo/ Adjumani refugee settlement with skills and knowledge to eradicate persistent cultural practices that harass and dismiss voices of women both in private and public spheres.  Using the acquired knowledge &amp; skills, youth will participate in the formulation and implementation of policies at district and national levels that directly impact refugees. Emphasis will be put on policies such as National Action Plan on UNSCR 1325/2250 (Women / Youth, Peace and Security), which recognises impacts of conflict on women.</narrative>
  </description>
